---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 15</p>
  <h1>Rooms &amp; <em>furniture</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Walk through a home and name what you see. Learn the <strong>rooms</strong> — <span class="ex">kitchen</span>, <span class="ex">bedroom</span>, <span class="ex">living room</span> — and the <strong>furniture</strong> in them — <span class="ex">sofa</span>, <span class="ex">bed</span>, <span class="ex">desk</span>. Then say where things are with <strong>there is / there are</strong> and small place words: <span class="ex">There is a lamp on the desk.</span> <span class="ex">There are two chairs in the kitchen.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">there is / there are</span>
    <span class="tag">in · on · under · next to</span>
    <span class="tag">8 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Read a short tour of an apartment.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>One thing vs. many; small place words.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match furniture to rooms, choose, and build.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe your own home, room by room.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Two words, one thing: a <span class="ex">sofa</span> is also a <span class="ex">couch</span>; a <span class="ex">refrigerator</span> is also a <span class="ex">fridge</span>. Both are correct and adult. We use <span class="ex">sofa</span> and <span class="ex">refrigerator</span> as the main words here.</p>

  <h2>Meet the home</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Rooms and the things inside them.</p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bed.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">bed</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/couch.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">couch</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/chair.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">chair</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/door.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">door</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/window.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">window</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/television.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">television</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/mirror.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">mirror</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/plant.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">plant</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/toilet.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">toilet</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/bathtub.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">bathtub</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/shower.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">shower</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/key.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">key</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/light.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">light</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/candle.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">candle</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/picture.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">picture</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/clock.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">clock</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/broom.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">broom</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/soap.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">soap</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/basket.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">basket</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/wastebasket.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">wastebasket</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/radio.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">radio</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/phone.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">phone</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A short tour of Mateo's apartment</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"This is my apartment. There is a sofa in the living room. There are two lamps next to the sofa. In the home office there is a desk, and there is a laptop on the desk. There are three chairs in the kitchen."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>When Mateo names <strong>one</strong> thing, he says <span class="ex">there is</span>. When he names <strong>two or three</strong>, he says something different. What changes?</li>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">on the desk</span>, <span class="ex">in the kitchen</span>, <span class="ex">next to the sofa</span>. These small words tell you <strong>where</strong>. Which one means "touching the top"?</li>
      <li>Which furniture word goes with the <strong>kitchen</strong>? Which goes with the <strong>home office</strong>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check — one thing or many?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Count the noun. One thing takes <b>is</b>; two or more takes <b>are</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is">is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a bed in the bedroom. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one bed)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> two lamps next to the sofa. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(two lamps)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a desk in the home office. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one desk)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>There <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="are" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> three chairs in the kitchen. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(three chairs)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: rooms, furniture, and where things are</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>First, the <strong>rooms</strong> in a home, and the furniture you usually find in each:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>room</th><th>furniture you usually find there</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>kitchen</b></td><td><b>stove</b>, <b>refrigerator</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">fridge</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>living room</b></td><td><b>sofa</b> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">couch</span>, <b>rug</b>, <b>bookshelf</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>bedroom</b></td><td><b>bed</b>, <b>closet</b>, <b>mirror</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>bathroom</b></td><td><b>mirror</b>, <b>shelf</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>dining room</b></td><td><b>table</b>, <b>chairs</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>home office</b></td><td><b>desk</b>, <b>lamp</b>, <b>chair</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>hallway</b> / <b>balcony</b></td><td>often empty, or one small <b>shelf</b> / <b>chair</b></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>Next, the small <strong>place words</strong>. They tell you exactly where a thing is:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>place word</th><th>meaning</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>in</b></td><td>inside something</td><td><span class="ex">The towels are in the closet.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>on</b></td><td>touching the top</td><td><span class="ex">The lamp is on the desk.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>under</b></td><td>below it</td><td><span class="ex">The rug is under the table.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>next to</b></td><td>beside it</td><td><span class="ex">The chair is next to the bed.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>behind</b></td><td>at the back of it</td><td><span class="ex">The closet is behind the door.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>between</b></td><td>in the middle of two</td><td><span class="ex">The lamp is between the bed and the wall.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>in front of</b></td><td>facing the front of it</td><td><span class="ex">The sofa is in front of the bookshelf.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>One thing or many? Use <span class="ex">There is a sofa</span> for one, <span class="ex">There are two chairs</span> for two or more. The verb follows the noun after it.</li>
      <li><span class="ex">in</span> the desk or <span class="ex">on</span> the desk? A book that sits on top is <span class="ex">on the desk</span>. A drawer holds things <span class="ex">in the desk</span>. For a book on top, <span class="ex">on</span> is correct.</li>
      <li>To ask, say <span class="ex">Where is the lamp?</span> for one thing and <span class="ex">Where are the keys?</span> for many. The short answer keeps the place word: <span class="ex">It's on the desk.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Match the furniture to its room</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Most furniture has a home of its own. Connect each thing to the room where you usually find it:</p>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game>
    <h3>Drill 1 — furniture → its usual room</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a piece of furniture, then tap the room it usually belongs in</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="stove">stove</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="bed">bed</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="sofa">sofa</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="desk">desk</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="stove" data-placeholder="kitchen">kitchen</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="bed" data-placeholder="bedroom">bedroom</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="sofa" data-placeholder="living room">living room</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="desk" data-placeholder="home office">home office</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the right place word</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Read the picture in your head, then pick the place word that matches the cue:</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2 — in / on / under / next to</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The cue in brackets tells you exactly where the thing is</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="in">in</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="on">on</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="under">under</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="next to">next to</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The lamp is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the desk. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(touching the top)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The towels are <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="in" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the closet. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(inside it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The rug is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="under" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the table. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(below it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The chair is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="next to" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bed. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(right beside it)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The mirror is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="on" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the wall. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(hanging on its surface)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="there is a lamp on the desk">
    <h3>Drill 3 — one thing, with a place word</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">One lamp, sitting on the desk in the home office. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="lamp">lamp</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="there">There</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="on">on</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="desk">desk</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="there are two chairs in the kitchen">
    <h3>Drill 4 — many things, with a room</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Two chairs, standing in the kitchen. Use <span class="ex">There are</span> for more than one. Build it, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="chairs">chairs</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="there">There</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="kitchen">kitchen</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="two">two</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="in">in</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="is" data-fix="There are two chairs." data-why="Two chairs is more than one, so the verb is are, not is.">
    <h3>Drill 5 — does the verb match the number?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. There are two chairs, not one.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="there">There</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="chairs">chairs.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="in" data-fix="The book is on the desk." data-why="The book sits on top of the desk, so the place word is on, not in.">
    <h3>Drill 6 — does the place word match?</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. The book sits on top of the desk.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="book">The book</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="in">in</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="desk">the desk.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7 — say where it is, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the object and its place. Say the full <span class="ex">There is / There are</span> sentence aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> a sofa · in the living room &nbsp;→&nbsp; full sentence</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There is a sofa in the living room.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> two lamps · next to the bed &nbsp;→&nbsp; full sentence</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There are two lamps next to the bed.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> a mirror · on the wall &nbsp;→&nbsp; full sentence</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There is a mirror on the wall.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> a rug · under the table &nbsp;→&nbsp; full sentence</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There is a rug under the table.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> three chairs · in the kitchen &nbsp;→&nbsp; full sentence</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>There are three chairs in the kitchen.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A hotel room</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“The hotel room is small but nice. There is a big bed and a comfortable couch. The bathroom has a bathtub and a large mirror. There is no television, but the window has a beautiful view.”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood a real room description.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a bathtub and a mirror">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What is in the bathroom?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a bathtub and a mirror">a bathtub and a mirror</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a bed and a couch">a bed and a couch</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a television">a television</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a television">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What is not in the room?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a television">a television</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a bed">a bed</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a window">a window</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the window">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. What has a beautiful view?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the window">the window</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the mirror">the mirror</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the couch">the couch</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your living room:</b> Name four things in your real living room. Say a full sentence for each. <span class="ex">There is a sofa. There is a rug under the table. There are two lamps.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your home office:</b> Describe where you work. <span class="ex">There is a desk next to the window. There is a lamp on the desk. There are three books on the shelf.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Where is it?</b> The teacher asks <span class="ex">Where is the lamp? Where are the chairs?</span> Answer with a place word. <span class="ex">It's on the desk. They're in the kitchen.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your apartment tour:</b> Give a short tour, room by room. <span class="ex">This is the kitchen. There is a stove and a refrigerator. This is the bedroom. There is a bed and a closet.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Spot the difference:</b> The teacher describes a room with one wrong detail. The student listens and corrects it. <span class="ex">No, the rug is under the table, not on the table.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For one thing I say <strong>There ______ a…</strong>. For two or more I say <strong>There ______ two…</strong>. Inside something is ______; touching the top is ______; below it is ______; beside it is ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say two true sentences about your own home: one with <strong>There is</strong> and one with <strong>There are</strong>, each with a place word.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can name rooms and furniture and say where things are with there is / there are and place words.">
    <h3>Final quiz — rooms, furniture, and where things are</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="is">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. There ___ a bed in the bedroom. (one bed)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="are">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. There ___ two lamps in the living room. (two lamps)</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="is">is</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="are">are</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="on">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. The laptop sits on top of the desk. The laptop is ___ the desk.</p>
